/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:48:<reference_puzzle index="3" source="eval" puzzle_id="3dc255db" lines="37-53">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:49:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:50:Eject content pixels from cup-shaped frames outward along each cup's tail direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:51:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:52:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:53:- bg = background. Hollow cup/Y/funnel frames, each a unique border color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:54:- Each cup has a convergent tail spike on one side and an open mouth on the opposite side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:55:- Content pixels (a single non-border color per cup) sit inside the cup's mouth interior.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:56:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:57:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:58:- For each cup, identify its tail spike and tail direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:59:- Erase all content pixels from the mouth interior.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:60:- Draw a straight line of content-colored pixels from the spike outward in the tail direction,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:61:  one pixel per erased content pixel; cells beyond the grid edge are dropped.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:62:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:63:Key insight: The tail spike is the unique convergent point whose outward direction is opposite
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:64:the mouth opening where the content lives.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:65:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:66:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:67:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:68:<reference_puzzle index="4" source="eval" puzzle_id="d8e07eb2" lines="29-47">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:69:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:70:Look up query glyphs in a reference table and mark whether they form a line.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:71:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:72:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:73:- Teal background with two full-width pink separator rows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:74:- Above the first separator is a query row of 5x5 glyph cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:75:- Between separators is a reference table of the same 5x5 cells; a glyph is
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:76:  identified by both its color and its 3x3 shape.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:77:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:78:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:79:- Green-fill the background inside every table cell whose glyph exactly
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:80:  appears in the query row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:81:- If the matched table cells form one complete row or one complete column,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:82:  also green-fill the query band and the bottom verdict band.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:83:- Otherwise leave the query band unchanged and fill the bottom verdict band red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:84:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:85:Key insight: The bottom color is not a count; it is the yes/no answer to
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:86:whether the queried glyphs align as a full row or column in the table.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:87:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:88:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:89:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:90:<reference_puzzle index="5" source="eval" puzzle_id="d59b0160" lines="39-54">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:91:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:92:Delete connected components whose colors match a legend swatch.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:93:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:94:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:95:- Background (bg) fills most of the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:96:- Top-left corner: a small square legend region bordered on its bottom and right edges by a single color; the interior holds a set of "target" colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:97:- Elsewhere: multicolored objects (4-connected components) on the bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:98:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:99:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:100:- Read the target color set from inside the legend border.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:101:- For each connected component, check whether it contains **all** target colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:102:- Erase (fill with bg) every component that does; leave all others unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:103:- Output grid is the same size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:104:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:105:Key insight: The legend acts as a filter specification — only components carrying the full color palette shown in the legend are removed.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:106:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:107:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:108:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:109:<reference_puzzle index="6" source="eval" puzzle_id="5dbc8537" lines="10-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:110:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:111:Fill rectangular cavities in a template shape by placing source sprites into matching holes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:112:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:113:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:114:- bg = most common color. A dominant "base" color forms a large frame/template with rectangular gaps.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:115:- Small colored sprites sit outside the template region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:116:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:117:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:118:- The base color (largest connected component excluding bg) defines the template bbox.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:119:- Each rectangular hole inside the template matches exactly one outside sprite by size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:120:- Place each sprite into its matching cavity; output is the filled template bbox.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:121:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:122:Key insight: Sprite bounding boxes match cavity dimensions exactly — it's a jigsaw-fit puzzle where each piece has a unique slot.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:123:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:124:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:125:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:126:<reference_puzzle index="7" source="eval" puzzle_id="21897d95" lines="283-301">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:127:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:128:Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:129:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:130:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:131:- The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:132:- Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:133:- Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:134:- An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:135:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:136:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:137:- For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:138:- The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:139:- For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:140:- All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:141:- A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:142:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:143:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:144:- The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:145:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:146:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:147:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:148:<reference_puzzle index="8" source="eval" puzzle_id="409aa875" lines="68-81">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:149:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:150:Fire projectiles from 3-pixel triangle sprites; mark collisions with maroon or blue.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:151:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:152:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:153:- bg = most common color. Non-bg 3-pixel sprites shaped as axis-aligned L's or diagonal V's.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:154:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:155:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:156:- Each triangle has an apex and an emission direction determined by its shape: L-shapes fire diagonally away from the missing corner; V-shapes fire along the axis away from the open side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:157:- A projectile lands exactly 5 cells from the apex in the emission direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:158:- If it hits an existing sprite, that entire sprite is recolored to maroon (9).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:159:- If two projectiles land on the same empty cell, that cell becomes blue (1); a lone projectile on empty bg paints maroon (9).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:160:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:161:Key insight: The triangle's orientation encodes both direction and target; dual-projectile collisions on open bg produce blue, not maroon.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:162:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:163:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:164:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:165:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="eval" puzzle_id="faa9f03d" lines="36-52">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:166:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:167:Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by replacing singleton markers, filling short orthogonal gaps, and redirecting yellow-marked arms to the edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:168:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:169:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:170:- A rectangular grid with a dominant background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:171:- Line colors form one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical stroke fragments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:172:- Marker colors are exactly those whose 4-connected components are all singleton pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:173:- Red singleton markers are missing line cells; yellow singleton markers are directional controls next to a line endpoint.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:174:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:175:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:176:- Assign every marker to the nearest visible line color in row/column line-of-sight, preferring an endpoint supported along that same axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:177:- For each line color, fill the gap between consecutive facing endpoints in a row or column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:178:- A yellow control erases the old straight arm on the far side of its endpoint and paints the same color from that endpoint through the control pixel to the grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:179:- At crossings, yellow-control rays win; otherwise an original-vs-filled crossing uses the more fragmented pre-repair line color, while pure filled crossings use the lower color id.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:180:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:181:Key insight: The singleton markers identify which sparse stroke fragments belong together; after they are colored, the intended lines are the axis-aligned gaps between facing endpoints, with yellow controls flipping one arm to the marked side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:182:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:183:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:184:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:185:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="eval" puzzle_id="7b5033c1" lines="7-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:186:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:187:Straighten a colored snake path into a single-column strip preserving pixel order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:188:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:189:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:190:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:191:- Non-bg pixels form a single 4-connected path (snake) with exactly two endpoints.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:192:- Each path pixel may be a different non-bg color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:193:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:194:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:195:- Find the two endpoints (cells with only one path neighbor) of the snake.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:196:- Begin at the top-left-most endpoint and trace the path cell by cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:197:- Output an (N×1) column listing each cell's color in traversal order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:198:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:199:Key insight: The path is a simple chain with no branches; choosing the top-left-most endpoint fixes a unique reading direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:200:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:201:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:202:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:203:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="eval" puzzle_id="20270e3b" lines="7-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:204:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:205:Connect two sprites using matching connector pixels, then tight-crop.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:206:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:207:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:208:- Background color `bg`, sprite color `obj`, connector color `ctrl` (small, 2 components).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:209:- Two main foreground sprites, plus possibly tiny detached pixels belonging to one sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:210:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:211:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:212:- Identify the **base** sprite (closest to grid top-left).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:213:- Translate the other sprite so its connector sits one cell above the base's connector.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:214:- Stamp the plug onto the base; remove connectors (recolor `ctrl` to `obj`).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:215:- Output is the tight crop around all non-background pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:216:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:217:Key insight: The connector pixels define the unique docking point and direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:218:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:219:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:220:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:221:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="eval" puzzle_id="195c6913" lines="37-52">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:222:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:223:Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:224:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:225:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:226:- Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:227:- Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:228:- A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:229:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:230:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:231:- Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:232:- On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:233:- Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:234:- If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:235:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:236:Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.
