/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:260:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:261:Transmit colored tokens along wire networks, converting each to its complementary 3×3 pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:262:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:263:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:264:- bg = background. Non-bg cells form wire networks and 3×3 tokens (solid blocks or X/diagonal patterns) near wire endpoints.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:265:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:266:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:267:- Every solid 3×3 token is replaced in-place by a diamond (center + 4 cardinal neighbors).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:268:- Each token near a wire endpoint sends its complement to the opposite endpoint: solid emits X, X emits diamond.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:269:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:270:Key insight: Token shape cycles solid → X → diamond; wires route each complement to the far end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:271:</description>
