/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:275:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:276:Fill the parallelogram-shaped region between parallel anti-diagonal line segments with red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:277:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:278:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:279:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:280:- One non-bg color forms short diagonal segments, each lying on a single anti-diagonal (r+c = const).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:281:- Segments come in parallel pairs bounding a region to be filled.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:282:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:283:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:284:- For each main-diagonal axis (r−c = const), collect anti-diagonal segments whose span covers that axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:285:- Sort those segments by their anti-diagonal index (r+c).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:286:- Fill all bg cells lying strictly between consecutive segment pairs along that axis with red (color 2).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:287:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:288:Key insight: The two diagonal directions decouple — segments sit on anti-diagonals, and filling sweeps along main diagonals between them, forming parallelogram regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:289:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:290:</reference_puzzle>
