/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:293:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:294:Fill rectangles between diagonal marker pairs using a color legend.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:295:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:296:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:297:- bg grid with a vertical legend at the bottom-left: each row is a (marker_color, fill_color) pair.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:298:- Scattered L-shaped corner markers of each marker color define opposite corners of axis-aligned rectangles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:299:- Some markers are solid 2×2 blocks instead of corner pairs.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:300:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:301:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:302:- Read legend bottom-to-top; for each entry find all pixels of that marker color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:303:- Determine which two bbox corners carry L-shaped anchors — the *other* diagonal defines the fill region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:304:- Fill the diamond (all shortest-path cells between those two corners) with the legend's fill color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:305:- Solid 2×2 marker blocks are simply recolored to the fill color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:306:- Later legend entries are protected from earlier fills.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:307:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:308:Key insight: The L-shaped anchors sit on the marker diagonal; the fill goes on the opposite diagonal of the bounding box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:309:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:310:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:311:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:312:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="eval" puzzle_id="aa4ec2a5" lines="52-66">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:313:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:314:Add red outlines around objects, and mark enclosed holes inside hollow objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:315:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:316:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:317:- A mostly uniform background contains one or more 4-connected foreground objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:318:- Some objects may enclose 4-connected background holes inside their bbox.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:319:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:320:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:321:- For every foreground component, draw a one-cell 8-neighborhood outline in red (2).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:322:- If a component has enclosed background holes, recolor the component to teal (8).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:323:- Fill those enclosed holes with magenta (6) before drawing the outline.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:324:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:325:Key insight: Holes are treated as part of the object for outlining, while only objects
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:326:that actually enclose holes get the teal/magenta interior recoloring.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:327:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/prompt.md:328:</reference_puzzle>
