/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:348:Extend each of two aligned rectangular marker objects toward the other, filling half of the gap across the full perpendicular span.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:349:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:350:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:351:- A dominant background contains exactly two solid, same-sized monochromatic rectangles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:352:- The rectangles share either the same row span or the same column span, with a background gap between their facing edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:353:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:354:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:355:- If the rectangles are side-by-side, color the left half of the inter-object gap across every row with the left object's color, and the right half with the right object's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:356:- If one rectangle is above the other, color the upper half of the gap across every column with the upper object's color, and the lower half with the lower object's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:357:- When the gap length is odd, leave the center row/column as background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:358:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:359:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:360:- The marker objects are endpoints of an axial corridor; their own size identifies the facing edge, while the filled corridor spans the whole grid perpendicular to that axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:361:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/3.md:362:<annotation>
