/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:352:Scale up a monochrome control sprite by stamping a polychrome tile at each filled pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:353:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:354:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:355:- bg = background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:356:- Two foreground objects (8-connected): a monochrome rectangular sprite with bg holes (control), and a polychrome square tile (block).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:357:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:358:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:359:- For each cell in the control sprite's bbox: if filled, stamp a copy of the block tile; if bg, leave a tile-sized bg region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:360:- Output grid dimensions are (control_h × tile_h) by (control_w × tile_w).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:361:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:362:Key insight: The control sprite acts as a binary mask that gets "pixel-scaled" by the tile — each pixel expands to a full tile copy or empty space.
