/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:49:Replace a corner L with a same-color right-triangle outline in the corresponding corner of an enlarged canvas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:50:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:51:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:52:- The input is a square grid with one background color and one foreground color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:53:- The foreground is a one-pixel-thick L inside a square bbox.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:54:- The L touches exactly one horizontal grid edge and one vertical grid edge, identifying a corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:55:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:56:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:57:- Fill a square output canvas of side 3n-2, where n is the input side length, with the background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:58:- Double the L leg length to get the triangle side length.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:59:- Draw the two perpendicular triangle legs on the same output corner edges and connect their free endpoints with the diagonal.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:60:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:61:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:62:- The input L encodes the corner, color, and side length of the triangle outline; the missing side is the diagonal between the L's two free endpoints.
