/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:89:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:90:The grid has a dominant background, solid 3x3 grey and/or pink squares, and maroon marker pixels or segments directly touching one side of exactly one square.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:91:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:92:Grey squares are erased; their adjacent maroon markers stay in place and stamp the nearest edge cell inside the grey square. Pink squares stay pink; their adjacent maroon markers disappear and stamp the corresponding cell on the square's middle row or middle column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:93:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/7.md:94:The side touched by a marker determines the projection: grey uses the near edge, while pink uses the centerline, preserving the marker's coordinate along that side.
