/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:48:Fill partitioned regions with concentric colored bands derived from marker pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:49:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:50:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:51:- Grid partitioned into regions by wall-colored lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:52:- Each region has a dominant base color and a few isolated marker pixels of other colors at varying depths from the region boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:53:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:54:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:55:- For each region, read marker colors ordered by their Chebyshev distance from the boundary to build a color palette.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:56:- If no marker sits on the boundary itself, the base color leads the palette.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:57:- Paint every cell with palette[distance mod palette_length], producing repeating concentric rectangular frames that radiate inward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:58:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:59:Key insight: Each marker's depth from the boundary defines its position in the cyclic palette; the pattern then tiles inward automatically.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:60:</description>
