/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:97:Fill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:98:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:99:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:100:- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:101:- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:102:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:103:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:104:- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:105:- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:106:- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:107:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:108:Key insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed917989826/3/codegen_prompts/5.md:109:</description>
